# Configuring Site Run

The [`site:run`](../run-mojo.html) goal serves the site from a local HTTP server and renders each page when it is requested, so you can edit a document and reload the page in the browser to see the change. It uses the HTTP server that the JDK provides; no servlet container is needed.

${esc.h}${esc.h} Start the server

From the directory of a single project, run:

```shell
mvn site:run
```

The server listens on `http://localhost:8080/` until you stop Maven with `Ctrl+C`. The log shows the address, then the source of each page as it is rendered:

```
[INFO] --- site:${project.version}:run (default-cli) @ scratch-parent ---
[INFO] Relativizing site links with respect to localized project URL: https://example.org/scratch/
[INFO] Configuring report plugin maven-project-info-reports-plugin:3.9.0
[INFO] Configured 2 reports for maven-project-info-reports-plugin:3.9.0: index, summary
[INFO] Skipped "About" report (maven-project-info-reports-plugin:3.9.0:index), file "index.html" already exists.
[INFO] Started site:run HTTP server on http://localhost:8080/
[INFO] index.html -> src/site/markdown/index.md (default locale)
[INFO] summary.html -> maven-project-info-reports-plugin:3.9.0:summary (default locale)
[INFO] Generating "Summary" report              --- maven-project-info-reports-plugin:3.9.0:summary
```

`site:run` serves one project. To preview the links between the modules of a multi-module site, stage it with [`site:stage`](../stage-mojo.html) instead, as described in [Building multi-module sites](https://maven.apache.org/guides/mini/guide-multimodule-site.html).

${esc.h}${esc.h} Change the host, the port or the working directory

The [`host`](../run-mojo.html${esc.hash}host) and [`port`](../run-mojo.html${esc.hash}port) parameters choose where the server listens. Both can be set on the command line:

```shell
mvn site:run -Dport=9000
```

If the port is already taken, the goal fails with `Error creating HTTP server on localhost:<port>: Address already in use`. Use `-Dport=0` to let the system pick a free port; the log then shows which one it chose.

Static resources, such as the skin and the files in `src/site/resources`, are copied to [`tempWebappDirectory`](../run-mojo.html${esc.hash}tempWebappDirectory), `target/site-webapp` by default. To set the parameters in the POM:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-site-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <port>9000</port>
          <tempWebappDirectory>${esc.d}{project.build.directory}/site-tempdir</tempWebappDirectory>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
  ...
</project>
```

With this configuration, `mvn site:run` serves the site on `http://localhost:9000/` and copies the static resources to `target/site-tempdir`.

${esc.h}${esc.h} Render the site to disk while you edit

[`site:auto-refresh`](../auto-refresh-mojo.html) is the alternative when you want files instead of a server: it renders the site once into `target/site`, then renders a document again whenever its source changes, until you press Enter. In batch mode (`-B`) it renders the site once and stops.
